//- SAY IT: covers, statements, lists, quotes, and the loud ones.

section(data-spine="Say it")

  section.divider
    h2 Say it
    p Covers, statements, lists and quotes.
    p templates/_cover.scss, templates/_statement.scss, components/_blocks.scss

  section.cover(data-spine-section="Covers")
    p.a-talk-by a talk by #{authorHandle}
    h1 The Title Goes Low
    p (and the subtitle is an aside)
    aside.notes
      ul
        li section.cover: byline at the top, title set low in Yrsa, subtitle as an aside. templates/_cover.scss.

  section.statement(data-spine-section="Statements")
    h2 One sentence, hung high and flush left.
    p.fragment The kicker lands after, quieter.
    aside.notes
      ul
        li section.statement with a p kicker. templates/_statement.scss.

  section.statement
    h2 Or the kicker is an aside.
    p.aside (said under the breath)
    aside.notes
      ul
        li p.aside makes the kicker the mono aside voice.

  section.statement
    h2 I like CSS.
    h2.fragment I like the browser.
    h2.fragment I like you.
    aside.notes
      ul
        li Several h2s stack as a build on one edge.

  section.statement.lead-in
    p The setup line comes first.
    h2.fragment Then the payoff lands.
    aside.notes
      ul
        li .statement.lead-in: a quiet p before the heading.

  section.statement.is-shout
    h2 The one line that earns it.
    aside.notes
      ul
        li .statement.is-shout: the loud register, in Yrsa. Once per talk, maybe twice.

  section.statement(data-background-image="img/gif/speed-driving.gif" data-background-size="cover" data-background-opacity="0.35")
    h2.strobe Speed round!
    p.aside (prefers-reduced-motion turns the strobe off)
    aside.notes
      ul
        li .strobe cycles the palette. components/_effects.scss.
        li data-background-opacity dims a busy picture so the words on it stay readable.

  section.statement
    h2 Do not #[span.blink blink].
    aside.notes
      ul
        li .blink on an inline span: it holds still, then blinks twice, like an eye.

  section(data-spine-section="Lists")
    h3 A heading with points that land
    ul
      li.fragment One at a time.
      li.fragment Each with a short rise.
      li.fragment Eased on a recorded spring.
    aside.notes
      ul
        li Plain ul with li.fragment. motion/_fragments.scss.

  section
    h3 Numbered steps
    ol
      li.fragment Write the thing.
      li.fragment Ship the thing.
      li.fragment Panic.
    aside.notes
      ul
        li Plain ol with li.fragment.

  section(data-spine-section="Quotes")
    blockquote
      p Any sufficiently advanced CSS is indistinguishable from JavaScript.
      cite Someone, probably
    aside.notes
      ul
        li blockquote + cite. The mark is Mustard, the cite Yrsa italic. components/_blocks.scss.

  section.statement(data-spine-section="Fragments")
    h2 Fragments with #[span.fragment.mark opinions].
    p #[span.fragment.strike It's fine.] #[span.fragment.bounce It's not fine.]
    aside.notes
      ul
        li .fragment.mark sweeps Focus Yellow behind a word, .fragment.strike draws a Rust line through, .fragment.bounce drops in from above.

  section(data-spine-section="Small print")
    h3 Small print and keys
    p Press #[kbd S] for speaker view, #[kbd F] for full screen.
    p.footnote * Your keyboard may vary.
    aside.notes
      ul
        li kbd, and .footnote (or sub.footnote) in the aside voice.
        li Press #[kbd S] for speaker view; notes like these show there.
